Five documents from eight parallel corpus sweeps plus two repo audits, all
fact-checked against FINDINGS.md by an adversarial pass (six errors found and
corrected before commit).

The headline is a contradiction, so it is the finding. The commissioning
directive asked why SDF papers were missing from the corpus. They are not
missing, and neither are Lorensen & Cline, van Gelder & Wilhelms, or Kobbelt
et al. — all three were reported ABSENT by sweep agents and all three are
downloaded, converted and embedded. Each ranks #1 on a targeted query and
returns with title, authors, doi and year all null. 37.3% of search hits are
unidentifiable this way; 100% of non-DOI stems are. Years are actively wrong
in 7 of 10 spot checks. The loss is in the catalog rather than in Qdrant:
broken rows carry only conversion and embedding blocks, no provenance at all.
Papers ingested through paper_download are intact; papers that arrived any
other way are invisible to search.

That bears directly on rule 5. "Look it up rather than guess" currently
fails about one time in three, which is how three foundational case-table
sources came to be believed absent.

Three corrections owed to documents already in this tree:

- Dual Contouring of Hermite Data is present at 10.1145/566570.566586. Three
  independent sweeps reported it absent citing 10.1145/566654.566586, which
  does not resolve. Any ticket carrying the second DOI has a bad citation.
- TetWild is a phantom catalog row (catalog_no_source), not an absent paper.
- The seam answer this corpus actually supports is transition cells. Ju 2002's
  "requires no crack patching" is now checkable — the paper is here — but has
  not been read against that question, so the DC-is-crack-free claim stays R.

Also recorded, because a null belongs in the log: DEMOS.md's example count was
expected to have drifted and has not. 36 claimed, 36 present.

Two results worth carrying forward. All 14 open tickets are blocked and four
of the blocks are the crate owner's decision, so the queue is currently a
queue of one — R-027a, an S, unblocked, and capable of dissolving R-027's L.
And a sweep over 9,425 documents plus a live provider search found no prior
art for stable identity of isosurface output elements without carrying state
across calls, which puts R-027a in unoccupied territory of the same shape as
V-43 and deserving the same care in the record.

Every claim in these documents is tiered. The coverage tables are M against
the live corpus; the novelty rows are R and none of them is a claim about
this crate's behaviour.

