+|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| 1 Tunnel test in dual cells | One extra quadratic solve per *ambiguous* cell only. **M-282 measured the face decider at 2.4%**; this is a similar order. | Neutral | Neutral | Safe — closed-form, no iteration, no hashing | Fixes a correctness defect; enables nothing new by itself |
+| 2 Union-find safety gate | Near-zero; runs only where a reposition is proposed | Neutral | One scratch forest per cell | Safe | Unlocks aggressive snapping |
+| 3 Randomised tet split | Zero — same work, different diagonal | Neutral | Zero | **Safe if the hash is of grid coordinates.** A PRNG would destroy golden hashes; a coordinate hash is a pure function | Better triangles on flat faces |
